{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1533239865,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNDcxNTI4OTk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2729","origin":"github"},"title":"API: composite command","message":"An idea for discussion, although not sure yet if effort worth it at this point of human evolution\n\nATM extensions could provide their additional commands to be added to the API.  That is great, but also adds toll on import time and also the \"length\" of the list of the commands etc.  I wondered if we should add support and RF for \"two level\" commands, e.g. instead of `datalad containers-run` after installation of `datalad-containers` (see XXX) we would get `datalad containers run`.\n\nThat later could be adopted for RFing `aggregate-metadata` into `metadata aggregate`, `extract-metadata` into `metadata extract`, `create-sibling` -\u003e `siblings create` etc  to make whole cmdline api more sensible\n\nAt Python level, such an API could also go through attributes of the (composite) command class, where `__call__()` would do what it does now (e.g. for `siblings`) and then submethods would implement their own commands:\n`metadata.aggregate`, `metadata.extract`, `siblings.create`","files":null}]}